# Anything that gets executed or parsed on the device must stay LF.  The
# Windows checkouts here run with core.autocrlf=true, which otherwise turns
# every .sh into CRLF in the working copy - and a CRLF shell script dies on
# Linux with "bad interpreter: /bin/bash^M".  See ngp45ht/README.md.
*.sh        text eol=lf
*.service   text eol=lf
*.timer     text eol=lf
*.rules     text eol=lf
*.py        text eol=lf
*.conf      text eol=lf
